          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Fig.7.3(a): A laboratory thermometer"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.093,
            0.618,
            0.115
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7.3.2 Laboratory thermometer"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.12,
            0.885,
            0.328
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "There are many types of laboratory thermometers but the one that might be available in your school laboratory may look like the one shown in Fig. 7.3a. It consists of a long, narrow, uniform glass tube which is sealed. At one end of the tube is a bulb which contains a liquid. Outside the bulb, in the tube, a narrow column of liquid can be seen. There is a Celsius scale marked along the tube. The liquid column rises or falls with change in temperature. The mark of the Celsius scale with which the top level of the liquid column coincides is the temperature reading."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.319,
            0.356,
            0.754,
            0.423
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "The liquid used in the laboratory thermometer is generally alcohol (coloured red to make it easily seen) or mercury."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.77,
            0.326,
            0.876,
            0.397
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 6,
              "bbox": [
                0.77,
                0.326,
                0.876,
                0.397
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_6.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.791,
            0.399,
            0.883,
            0.442
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do you know?",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.255,
            0.464,
            0.545,
            0.488
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Activity 7.3: Let us observe"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.253,
            0.497,
            0.883,
            0.539
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let us try to find the temperature range of a given laboratory thermometer."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.544,
            0.604,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Take a laboratory thermometer and observe it carefully."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.256,
            0.61,
            0.572,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Note down the following:"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.3,
            0.637,
            0.55,
            0.701
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the lowest temperature it can measure?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.342,
            0.723,
            0.556,
            0.789
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What is the highest temperature it can measure?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.73,
            0.537,
            0.792,
            0.58
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 14,
              "bbox": [
                0.73,
                0.537,
                0.792,
                0.58
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_7_image_14.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.693,
            0.587,
            0.828,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Precautions"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.675,
            0.607,
            0.849,
            0.666
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "to be taken while using a laboratory thermometer"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.301,
            0.81,
            0.562,
            0.853
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "So, the range of this thermometer is"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 18,
          "bbox": [
            0.644,
            0.67,
            0.865,
            0.748
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Handle with care. If it hits against some hard object, it can break."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 19,
          "bbox": [
            0.644,
            0.751,
            0.867,
            0.792
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Do not hold it by the bulb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 20,
          "bbox": [
            0.254,
            0.858,
            0.883,
            0.902
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Now look at the thermometer shown in Fig. 7.3a carefully. Can you tell its range? Its range is from "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "- 1 0 \\; ^ { \\circ } \\mathrm { C }"
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " to "
            },
            {
              "type": "equation_inline",
              "content": "{ \\tt 1 1 0 }   ^ { \\circ } \\mathsf { C } ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "footer",
